  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 469(g)(3), when a passive activity is disposed of via installment sale, suspended losses are released proportionally as gain is recognized. Year-one gain is $100,000 x 40% = $40,000, which is one-third of total $120,000 gain, so $60,000 x ($40,000 / $120,000) = $20,000 of suspended losses is allowed.
Wrong (A): The installment method defers both gain recognition and the proportional release of suspended losses, so the full $60,000 is not deductible in 2026.
Wrong (B): Suspended losses begin releasing in the first year gain is recognized, not when the final installment is received.
Wrong (D): The $60,000 of suspended losses does not all offset the $40,000 gain; only the proportional share ($20,000) is released in year one.$EXPL$
